{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I’m Dr. ___. You’re here today for your scheduled IVIG infusion, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve had trouble with the last two infusions—bad headaches and high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You were switched to a different type called Privigen this time because it’s lower in solutes and may be easier to tolerate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. My allergist thought this one might be better. But I’m still nervous—last time I had chest pressure like a heart issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor you very closely. We’ll start the infusion tomorrow morning, and we’ll give you acetaminophen and Benadryl beforehand to help prevent reactions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. And my blood pressure—we’ve been adjusting that lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re on valsartan and metoprolol, which we’ll continue. We’ll check your vitals frequently, especially during the infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I also get dizzy when I stand up—orthostatic hypotension. Should I be careful with fluids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll keep you on IV fluids as needed. We don’t want you getting dehydrated, especially with your mitochondrial condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. My kidney function has been a little off too—last time they said something about acidosis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw a mild acidosis on your labs, likely related to dehydration. We’ll keep an eye on your electrolytes and kidney values."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. So no changes to my usual meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’re continuing everything as is—your aspirin, Plavix, statin, Nexium, all of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want anything messing with my heart stability."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-01-23 15:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching that closely. Your EKG this morning showed sinus bradycardia, but it’s stable and not concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-01-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re going to start your IVIG infusion in about an hour. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-01-24 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A bit anxious, but okay. No dizziness or chest pain so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-01-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go slow with the infusion rate to minimize side effects. We’ve given you Benadryl and Tylenol already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-01-24 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. Last time my blood pressure spiked to 170 over 110. I hope this doesn’t happen again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-01-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring it every 15 minutes at first. If it starts to rise, we’ll slow the infusion or pause it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-01-24 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about 45 minutes into the infusion. Your blood pressure just went up to 180 systolic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-01-24 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a little chest tightness—not like my usual angina, but pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-01-24 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, we’re slowing the infusion. Your EKG shows no changes, so this isn’t a heart attack. It’s likely a reaction to the IVIG."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-01-24 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. The room also feels like it’s spinning a bit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-01-24 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be from the Benadryl or the blood pressure change. We’ll keep monitoring. Try to stay lying down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-01-24 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has come down to 150 over 90, and the chest tightness is gone. We’re resuming the infusion at a slower rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-01-24 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I feel more stable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-01-24 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve completed the infusion. We’ll keep observing you for a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-01-24 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel okay now—no dizziness or chest pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-01-25 01:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I’m having chest tightness again and shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-01-25 01:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re checking your oxygen—it’s 98% on room air. Blood pressure is 160 over 95. No EKG changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-01-25 01:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m not hypoxic, but it’s uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-01-25 01:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you supplemental oxygen for comfort. This seems like a delayed reaction, but it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-01-25 02:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your symptoms have resolved. We’ll continue to monitor overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-01-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your vitals have been stable overnight. We think you’re ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-01-26 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Did the IVIG help overall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-01-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you received the full dose. It’s important for your immune system. But you did have a hypertensive reaction and chest tightness, so we’ll discuss with your allergist which product works best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-01-26 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I still go back to my regular doctor for a check-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-01-26 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, definitely. Please follow up with your PCP to monitor your blood pressure. No changes to your medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-01-26 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-01-26 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay hydrated, and call if you have chest pain, severe headache, or dizziness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-01-26 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I feel much better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-01-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reviewed your labs—your kidney function is stable, and the mild acidosis has improved with fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-01-26 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to hear. I’ll keep up with my IV fluids at home as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-01-26 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your allergist may consider lowering the dose or extending the interval between infusions to reduce side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-01-26 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’d prefer fewer side effects even if it means more frequent visits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-01-26 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll communicate that. Otherwise, you’re cleared to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-01-26 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate the careful monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-01-26 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just confirming—no medication changes, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. Continue all your home medications as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my mitochondrial myopathy and heart disease are still stable?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, both remained stable during your stay. No new cardiac events."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ll follow up with my cardiologist soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good plan. Stay in touch with your team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling ready to head home now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve completed all checks. You’re discharged home in stable condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and stay well-hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2186-01-26 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you next time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-01-23 15:11:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-01-26 13:47:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of mitochondrial myopathy, coronary artery disease, and hypogammaglobulinemia was admitted for a scheduled IVIG infusion using Privigen, a low osmolar agent, due to prior adverse reactions with other formulations. During the infusion, he developed hypertension with systolic pressure up to 200 and transient chest tightness, which was distinct from his usual anginal symptoms and not associated with EKG changes. He also experienced dizziness and a delayed episode of chest tightness and shortness of breath, which resolved without intervention. His blood pressure was managed by slowing the infusion rate, and no medication changes were made. His mitochondrial myopathy and cardiac conditions remained stable. Mild acidosis and dehydration improved with supportive care. He was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to follow up on blood pressure and discuss infusion tolerance with his allergist.",
    "problems": [
      "Hypogammaglobulinemia, unspecified",
      "Acidosis",
      "Other myopathies",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty status",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Unspecified disorder of kidney and ureter",
      "Orthostatic hypotension",
      "Dehydration"
    ]
  }
}
